## 4. Monitor the Blob Cleanup / Garbage Collection Job

### Key tables to watch

| Table | What it holds | Shrinks during GC? |
|-------|--------------|---------------------|
| `blob` | All registry blobs (layers, configs) | Yes — unlinked blobs get deleted |
| `artifact_blob` | Links artifacts to their blobs | Yes — stale links removed |
| `artifact` | Image manifests/artifacts | Yes — if tags were deleted |
| `artifact_trash` | Artifacts marked for deletion | Grows first, then empties |
| `project_blob` | Per-project blob references | Yes |
| `task` | Job/task records (scan, GC, replication) | Old completed tasks accumulate |
| `execution` | Parent execution records | Old completed executions accumulate |

### Check table sizes (run periodically to track shrinkage)
```sql
-- Table sizes sorted by size
SELECT
    schemaname || '.' || relname AS table_name,
    pg_size_pretty(pg_total_relation_size(relid)) AS total_size,
    pg_size_pretty(pg_relation_size(relid)) AS data_size,
    pg_size_pretty(pg_total_relation_size(relid) - pg_relation_size(relid)) AS index_size,
    n_live_tup AS live_rows,
    n_dead_tup AS dead_rows
FROM pg_stat_user_tables
ORDER BY pg_total_relation_size(relid) DESC
LIMIT 20;

-- Just the key Harbor tables
SELECT
    relname AS table_name,
    pg_size_pretty(pg_total_relation_size(relid)) AS total_size,
    n_live_tup AS live_rows,
    n_dead_tup AS dead_rows
FROM pg_stat_user_tables
WHERE relname IN ('blob', 'artifact_blob', 'artifact', 'artifact_trash',
                  'project_blob', 'task', 'execution', 'scan_report')
ORDER BY pg_total_relation_size(relid) DESC;
```

### Track blob cleanup progress
```sql
-- Total blobs vs unlinked blobs (blobs with no artifact reference)
SELECT
    (SELECT count(*) FROM blob) AS total_blobs,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM blob
     WHERE id NOT IN (SELECT blob_id FROM artifact_blob)) AS orphan_blobs;

-- Artifacts in trash (waiting to be cleaned)
SELECT count(*) FROM artifact_trash;

-- Blob count over time — run this every 10-15 min to see if count drops
SELECT count(*) AS blob_count, pg_size_pretty(sum(size)) AS total_blob_size
FROM blob;

-- Recently deleted blobs (if GC is working, this query returns fewer results over time)
SELECT count(*) FROM artifact_blob
WHERE artifact_id NOT IN (SELECT id FROM artifact);
```

### Check the GC execution status
```sql
-- GC job executions
SELECT id, vendor_type, status, trigger, start_time, end_time,
       end_time - start_time AS duration
FROM execution
WHERE vendor_type = 'GARBAGE_COLLECTION'
ORDER BY start_time DESC
LIMIT 10;

-- GC tasks detail
SELECT t.id, t.status, t.status_code, t.status_message,
       t.creation_time, t.update_time,
       t.update_time - t.creation_time AS duration
FROM task t
JOIN execution e ON t.execution_id = e.id
WHERE e.vendor_type = 'GARBAGE_COLLECTION'
ORDER BY t.creation_time DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

