## 5. Clean Up Old Job Records (the `task` and `execution` tables bloat)

```sql
-- How many old task/execution records exist
SELECT
    (SELECT count(*) FROM task) AS total_tasks,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM task WHERE creation_time < now() - interval '30 days') AS old_tasks,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM execution) AS total_executions,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM execution WHERE start_time < now() - interval '30 days') AS old_executions;

-- Delete old completed tasks (> 30 days)
DELETE FROM task
WHERE status IN ('Success', 'Error', 'Stopped')
  AND creation_time < now() - interval '30 days';

-- Delete old completed executions (> 30 days)
DELETE FROM execution
WHERE status IN ('Success', 'Error', 'Stopped')
  AND start_time < now() - interval '30 days';

-- VACUUM after large deletes to reclaim space
VACUUM ANALYZE task;
VACUUM ANALYZE execution;
```

