## 6. Database Health & Space Reclamation

```sql
-- Overall database size
SELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_database_size('registry')) AS db_size;

-- Check for bloat (dead tuples needing VACUUM)
SELECT relname, n_dead_tup, n_live_tup,
       round(n_dead_tup::numeric / greatest(n_live_tup, 1) * 100, 2) AS dead_pct
FROM pg_stat_user_tables
WHERE n_dead_tup > 1000
ORDER BY n_dead_tup DESC;

-- Run VACUUM on bloated tables
VACUUM ANALYZE blob;
VACUUM ANALYZE artifact_blob;
VACUUM ANALYZE artifact;
VACUUM ANALYZE scan_report;

-- Full vacuum (locks table but reclaims disk space to OS — use during maintenance)
-- VACUUM FULL blob;
```

