## 7. Recommended Monitoring Approach

**While the cleanup job runs, execute this sequence every 10-15 minutes:**

```sql
-- Snapshot query — run repeatedly and compare
SELECT
    now() AS checked_at,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM blob) AS blob_count,
    (SELECT pg_size_pretty(sum(size)) FROM blob) AS blob_total_size,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM artifact_trash) AS trash_count,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM artifact_blob) AS artifact_blob_links,
    (SELECT pg_size_pretty(pg_database_size('registry'))) AS db_size,
    (SELECT count(*) FROM pg_stat_activity) AS active_connections;
```

**What to look for:**
- `blob_count` should decrease over time
- `trash_count` should go to 0 (artifacts fully cleaned)
- `db_size` may not shrink until you run `VACUUM FULL` (regular VACUUM marks space reusable but doesn't return it to OS)
- `active_connections` should stay well under `max_connections`

