## 8. Quick Fixes for Max Connections

If you can't change Postgres config immediately:

```bash
# Check current setting from outside
kubectl exec -it -n harbor <db-pod> -- psql -U postgres -c "SHOW max_connections;"

# Increase via postgresql.conf (requires restart)
kubectl exec -it -n harbor <db-pod> -- bash -c \
  "echo 'max_connections = 300' >> /var/lib/postgresql/data/postgresql.conf"

# Restart the database pod
kubectl delete pod -n harbor <db-pod>
```

For a permanent fix, set in Harbor Helm values:
```yaml
database:
  type: internal
  internal:
    # Add to extraEnvVars or via a custom postgresql.conf
    password: "..."
```

Or better, tune Harbor components to use fewer connections via `core` and `jobservice` environment variables.

