## 11. Investigation Sequence (Step-by-Step)

1. **Connect** to the Harbor PostgreSQL pod (Section 1)
2. **Assess connections** — run Section 2 queries to check if max_connections is the bottleneck
3. **Check GC status** — run Section 4 GC execution queries to confirm the job is running/completed
4. **Baseline snapshot** — run the Section 7 snapshot query and note the numbers
5. **Check table sizes** — run Section 4 table size queries
6. **Wait 10-15 min**, re-run the snapshot query — compare blob_count and trash_count
7. **Check scanning** — run Section 3 queries to find stuck/failed scans
8. **Check S3** — run Section 9 bucket size commands
9. **After GC completes** — clean old job records (Section 5), vacuum (Section 6), verify S3 reduction (Section 9)
10. **If space didn't shrink** — run `VACUUM FULL` on large tables during a maintenance window
